You can try a few things:
Define a schedule for the pool, as I did in my example, instead of calling set_capacity with a separate generator, because this could lead to race conditions.
Use get_capacity() - get_server_count() instead of just get_capacity() to select resources, because you may have several shifts with some capacity, but some may be full already.
Better yet, use the built-in policy "random-available", which is what you are doing if I understood it correctly.
Iñaki

